From 0459ee17e7aafde6ffe7090872df9473bee9b630 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:39:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Classify inconclusive VM failures and certify only bound
 deterministic block failures

Integration note (2026-10-15): the original source commit had no message body.
This maintenance explanation is added by the series integrator without changing
its source diff. Local cryptographic-provider, host-work and unsupported execution
failures become inconclusive, while bound deterministic block failures produce
an opaque proof carrying block, parent, profile and pre-block UTXO root. The
validator profile digest moves unchanged into the block transition layer.
Early header failures conservatively provide no proof. Focused VM, ordinary,
complete-block and signed-runner checks pass; downstream recovery and full-tree
evidence are recorded separately in the implementation plan.

